description:
FOUND s496a (Opus, 2026-09-26) while shipping #2372 (a regex compile error now DIES).

POSSESSIVE QUANTIFIERS (`X++`, `X*+`, `X?+`, `X{n,m}+`) were never translated: cl-ppcre rejects them ("Quantifier '+' not allowed"), and before #2372 that rejection was a stderr WARNING plus a no-match, so every possessive pattern silently never matched.  Since #2372 it is a trappable die at the match.  Neither is perl.

Minimal reproducer (perl 5.40.3 vs PCL):
    my @r;
    push @r, eval { ("aab" =~ /^a++b/) ? 1 : 0 } // "died";
    push @r, eval { ("aab" =~ /^[a]++b/) ? 1 : 0 } // "died";
    push @r, eval { ("aa" =~ /^a++a/) ? 1 : 0 } // "died";
    push @r, eval { ("ab" =~ /^\w++$/) ? 1 : 0 } // "died";
    print "@r\n";
  perl:             1 1 0 1
  PCL b6560c21:     0 0 0 0  (+ four "Regex syntax error" warnings)
  PCL s496a:        died died died died

FIX SHAPE: perl defines `X++` as `(?>X+)` (perlre "Possessive quantifiers": `X*+` = `(?>X*)`, `X++` = `(?>X+)`, `X?+` = `(?>X?)`, `X{n,m}+` = `(?>X{n,m})`).  A rewrite pass in perl-regex-to-ppcre needs the extent of the quantified ATOM (a char, an escape, a bracket class, a group) -- one forward scan in the style of %pcl-expand-hv-escapes.  Probe the breaking cases: `\++` (escaped plus then a quantifier), `[+]+`, `a{2}+`, possessive after a group `(ab)++`, inside a class (literal).


COST RAISED (s496a member 7, s499, 2026-09-27): qr// now compiles EAGERLY (Fable ruling), so a possessive inside a qr dies AT THE qr -- outside the eval that used to trap it at the match.  t/re/pat_rt_report.t line 401 `unlike("\xc4\xc4\xc4", qr/(\x{100}++)/, ...)` now aborts the file: companion 2431/26 -> 110/4 (2,321 rows behind this one construct; A/B vs a 0ab64a45 extraction).  Probe: `my $q = qr/(\x{100}++)/; print "made\n"` perl prints made, s496a dies.  This task now OWNS those rows; fixing it should restore pat_rt_report.t to >= 2431 ok.

=== DONE (s499e) ===
Possessive quantifiers are rewritten into perl's own definition `(?>X+)` / `(?>X*)` / `(?>X?)` / `(?>X{n,m})` in the ONE runtime rewrite scan (`%pcl-expand-hv-escapes` renamed `%pcl-rewrite-scan`; pre-test `%pcl-has-possessive`; cache miss only).  The atom is a character, an escape through its lexer extent, a bracket class, or a balanced group; no atom / a following quantifier = copied (`a++*` dies as perl's "Nested quantifiers").  ir-spec Â§10-poss.
Probe table 65 rows perl -> base -> tree: every possessive row equal to perl, incl. the breaking cases; semantic pair "aaa" =~ /a++a/ 0 vs /a+a/ 1.  Guards Pl/t/regexp-subst-01.t rows 49-50 (inverse-verified on 2b2db885).
